# SF Apartment Finder Cron Job Examples
#
# To use:
# 1. Edit the paths below to match your installation
# 2. Choose a schedule that works for you
# 3. Add to your crontab: crontab -e
# 4. Paste the desired cron job configuration
#
# Cron Format:
# * * * * * command to execute
# │ │ │ │ │
# │ │ │ │ └─── day of week (0-7) (Sunday=0 or 7)
# │ │ │ └────── month (1-12)
# │ │ └─────────── day of month (1-31)
# │ └──────────────── hour (0-23)
# └───────────────────── minute (0-59)

# ============================================
# CONFIGURATION - UPDATE THESE PATHS
# ============================================
PROJECT_DIR=/home/user/sf_apartment_finder
PYTHON_PATH=/home/user/sf_apartment_finder/venv/bin/python

# ============================================
# DAILY SCHEDULES
# ============================================

# Run daily at 9:00 AM
0 9 * * * cd $PROJECT_DIR && $PYTHON_PATH main.py >> logs/cron.log 2>&1

# Run daily at 6:00 AM
# 0 6 * * * cd $PROJECT_DIR && $PYTHON_PATH main.py >> logs/cron.log 2>&1

# Run daily at 8:30 AM
# 30 8 * * * cd $PROJECT_DIR && $PYTHON_PATH main.py >> logs/cron.log 2>&1

# ============================================
# MULTIPLE TIMES PER DAY
# ============================================

# Run twice daily (9 AM and 6 PM)
# 0 9,18 * * * cd $PROJECT_DIR && $PYTHON_PATH main.py >> logs/cron.log 2>&1

# Run three times daily (8 AM, 12 PM, 6 PM)
# 0 8,12,18 * * * cd $PROJECT_DIR && $PYTHON_PATH main.py >> logs/cron.log 2>&1

# ============================================
# WEEKDAY ONLY
# ============================================

# Run Monday-Friday at 9 AM
# 0 9 * * 1-5 cd $PROJECT_DIR && $PYTHON_PATH main.py >> logs/cron.log 2>&1

# ============================================
# WEEKLY SCHEDULES
# ============================================

# Run every Monday at 9 AM
# 0 9 * * 1 cd $PROJECT_DIR && $PYTHON_PATH main.py >> logs/cron.log 2>&1

# Run every Sunday at 10 AM
# 0 10 * * 0 cd $PROJECT_DIR && $PYTHON_PATH main.py >> logs/cron.log 2>&1

# ============================================
# TESTING
# ============================================

# Run every 5 minutes (for testing only!)
# */5 * * * * cd $PROJECT_DIR && $PYTHON_PATH main.py >> logs/cron.log 2>&1

# Run every hour at minute 0
# 0 * * * * cd $PROJECT_DIR && $PYTHON_PATH main.py >> logs/cron.log 2>&1

# ============================================
# SETUP INSTRUCTIONS
# ============================================
#
# 1. Update PROJECT_DIR and PYTHON_PATH above
# 2. Choose a schedule from the examples
# 3. Open crontab editor: crontab -e
# 4. Copy the desired cron line (uncomment it)
# 5. Save and exit
# 6. Verify: crontab -l
#
# To view cron logs:
#   tail -f /home/user/sf_apartment_finder/logs/cron.log
#
# To check system cron logs:
#   grep CRON /var/log/syslog
#
